</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.2.2 </span>Generalizability and Scalability of HARMO</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To verify that HARMO is not limited to a specific setup, we test its ”plug-and-play” capability and scalability. As shown in Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.2.2 Generalizability and Scalability of HARMO ‣ 4.2 Results and Analysis ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ Beyond Monolithic Rewards: A Hybrid and Multi-Aspect Reward Optimization for MLLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, when HARMO is integrated with a model trained with fine-grained, token-level rewards, it still provides a notable overall improvement of 5.76%. Furthermore, when applied to the larger Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct model, HARMO delivers an even greater enhancement of 6.55%. These results confirm HARMO’s robustness and its ability to serve as a versatile enhancement for different reward schemes and model sizes.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S4.T4.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:67.9pt;vertical-align:-32.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-121.8pt,20.8pt) scale(0.620042887672178,0.620042887672178) ;">
