</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduced HARMO, a novel reward optimization framework that advances reinforcement learning beyond monolithic signals by integrating a hybrid of deterministic and learned rewards with a generalized length penalty to control verbosity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our evaluation demonstrates that HARMO significantly enhances complex reasoning, achieving a 9.5% overall and a 16% mathematical performance gain over a strong baseline while maintaining robustness on vision-specific tasks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This work highlights the critical role of multi-faceted reward modeling in stabilizing RL training and improving reward accuracy. HARMO provides a strong foundation for future research, such as dynamic reward weighting or self-improving systems where agents learn to refine their own reward functions, paving the way for more robust and adaptable AI.</p>
</div>
</section>
